binary

; The data part of a segwit address (BIP-173, BIP-350) as the 5-bit symbols it
; is: a witness version, the program in octets -- which start after the
; version's 5 bits, in the middle of an octet -- the zero bits that fill the
; last symbol, and the 6-symbol checksum.
segwit = version:5 ?(version <= 16)
         program:[(remaining - 30) / 8]
         ?(len(program) >= 2 && len(program) <= 40)
         ?(version != 0 || len(program) == 20 || len(program) == 32)
         ?(remaining - 30 < 5) pad:bits(remaining - 30) ?(pad == 0)
         checksum:30
